.TH YABI 1 "2026-11-01" "yabi 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
yabi \- yet another bootsplash implementation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B yabi
[\fIoptions\fR] \fIcommand\fR [\fIarguments\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B yabi
shows a boot splash on the Linux framebuffer and lets the boot scripts drive
it. It starts
.BR fbv (1)
with a control socket and leaves it running; every later call sends one
command to it and exits. There is no daemon.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR start " [\fItheme\fR]"
Start fbv with the theme's animation, \fBdefault\fR when none is given, and
wait until it answers. A theme with mode \fBprogress\fR starts on its first
frame.
.TP
.BI progress " percent"
Move a progress animation to \fIpercent\fR (0 to 100). Forward moves step
through the frames at the animation's pace.
.TP
.BI frame " n"
Show frame \fIn\fR of the animation.
.TP
.BR pause ", " resume
Stop and restart the animation.
.TP
.BI show " file"
Switch to another image or animation.
.TP
.BI theme " theme"
Switch to another theme.
.TP
.B status
Print the current frame, the frame count and whether the animation is paused.
.TP
.B ping
Exit 0 when the splash is running.
.TP
.B quit
Close the splash and wait until fbv has exited, so the framebuffer is free.
.TP
.BR watch " [\fIdir\fR...]"
Follow the boot in the background until the splash is gone: move the progress
as the executable \fBS??*\fR scripts of the init directories run, in the
order of the directories and of the names. Under OpenRC the progress follows
the started services of the sysinit, boot and default runlevels instead.
Without directories it follows systemd when systemd runs, reading its own
boot progress after every finished job, and /etc/init.d otherwise. It sleeps
until something happens and changes nothing in the boot; \fBS01yabi\fR or
\fByabi-start.service\fR start it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-socket " \fIpath\fR"
Control socket, /run/yabi.sock by default or \fB$YABI_SOCKET\fR.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-fbv " \fIpath\fR"
fbv program to start, \fBfbv\fR from \fB$PATH\fR by default or \fB$YABI_FBV\fR.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-themes " \fIdir\fR"
Directory holding the themes.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-timeout " \fIms\fR"
How long to wait for fbv, 3000 by default.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-graphics
For \fBstart\fR: leave the console in text mode.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-retain
For \fBquit\fR: keep the splash on screen and the console in graphics mode
for the program taking over the display.
.SH THEMES
A theme is a directory, named or given as a path containing a slash, holding
\fBtheme.conf\fR and its animation:
.PP
.nf
# comment
animation = boot.gif   # relative to the theme directory
mode = progress        # progress or loop
scale = none           # none, shrink or fit
.fi
.PP
In \fBprogress\fR mode the animation holds the frame set by \fBprogress\fR;
an animation of 101 frames gives one frame per percent. In \fBloop\fR mode it
plays freely.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 done, 1 failed, 2 usage error, 3 splash not running.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
yabi start
yabi progress 30
yabi quit
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fbv (1)
